title: Friends in Moscow
subtitle: Every German faction has someone in the Russian leadership.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: rf_moscow
view-if: rf_patron_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; rf_patron_timer = 4

= Friends in Moscow

The Russian leaders each have their German friends. Whom the party listens to decides whom Moscow will back.

- @radek
- @zinoviev
- @stalin

@radek
title: Lean on Karl Radek, the International's expert on Germany.
subtitle: Moscow warms to the <span class="f-right">Right</span>.
on-arrival: {!
window.RF.lean(Q, {right: 2});
Q.right_moscow += 7;
Q.moscow_trust += 2;
!}

Radek knows Germany better than any Russian leader and has defended Brandler before. He will speak for the party's moderates.

@zinoviev
title: Court Grigory Zinoviev, chairman of the International.
subtitle: Moscow warms to the <span class="f-left">Left</span>.
on-arrival: {!
window.RF.lean(Q, {left: 2});
Q.left_moscow += 7;
Q.moscow_trust += 2;
!}

Zinoviev is happy to have a German faction of his own, and Fischer and Maslow are happy to be it.

@stalin
title: Cultivate the General Secretary's people.
subtitle: Moscow warms to <span class="f-stalin">Thälmann</span>, slowly while Stalin's word counts for little in the International.
on-arrival: {!
window.RF.lean(Q, {stalin: 2});
Q.stalin_moscow += Q.year >= 1924 ? 8 : 4;
Q.moscow_trust += 2;
!}

Stalin runs the Russian party's machine but has little say in the International yet. His people are building a network, and they are looking for Germans.
